ents (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Fluorine reacts with dilute $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ and forms a gaseous product $A$. The bond angle in the molecule of $A$ is","options":["$104^{\\circ} 40^{\\prime}$","$103^{\\circ}$","$107^{\\circ}$","$109^{\\circ} 28^{\\prime}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\quad 2 \\mathrm{~F}_{2}+2 \\underset{\\text { dilute }}{\\mathrm{NaOH}} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NaF}+\\underset{(A)}{\\mathrm{OF}_{2}} \\uparrow+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$\nThe structure of ' $A^{\\prime}\\left(\\mathrm{OF}_{2}\\right)$ is as\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252FcMytZ8OQwVmvnLOeZPI334erOV55rr1itkEBu14IgSk.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FcMytZ8OQwVmvnLOeZPI334erOV55rr1itkEBu14IgSk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FcMytZ8OQwVmvnLOeZPI334erOV55rr1itkEBu14IgSk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\n$\\sigma$ bonds made by $\\mathrm{O}=2$\nDue to repulsion between two lone pairs of electrons, its shape gets distorted. Therefore, the bond angle in the molecule is $103^{\\circ}$.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2009","_marksId":"64e458d3ec226f2f4360a63c"},{"id":116340,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Match List I (Substances) with List II (Processes employed in the manufacture of the substances) and select the correct option.\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252FlxE8aojIT2suQo7nZH0axgqu4rAXVtV3ivTEdK7aqGk.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FlxE8aojIT2suQo7nZH0axgqu4rAXVtV3ivTEdK7aqGk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FlxE8aojIT2suQo7nZH0axgqu4rAXVtV3ivTEdK7aqGk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\nCodes:\n$\\begin{array}{llll}\\mathrm{A} & \\mathrm{B} & \\mathrm{C} & \\mathrm{D} \\\\ \\end{array}$","options":["1  4  2  3","1  2  3  4","4  3  2  1","4  2  3  1"],"answer":3,"solution":"Contact process is used for sulphuric acid, steel is manufactured by Bessemer's process, Leblanc process is used for the production of $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ while Haber's process is used for $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ production.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2012","_marksId":"64e458f9ec226f2f4360a7b0"},{"id":116341,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Reaction of $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{PhMgBr}$ would give","options":["bromobenzene","chlorobenzene","triphenylphosphine","dichlorobenzene"],"answer":2,"solution":"In a reaction the alkyl part of grignard reagent acts as a nucleophile as carbon is more electronegative than magnesium. Hence the alkyl part will get attached to the electron deficient species.\nIn $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$, chlorine is more electronegative than phosphorous.\nHence the $\\mathrm{Ph}^{-}$will attack the phosphorous in $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$ to form organic phosphine with formula $\\mathrm{Ph}_{3} \\mathrm{P}3 \\mathrm{PhMgBr}+\\mathrm{PCl}_{3} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Ph}_{3} \\mathrm{P}+3 \\mathrm{MgBrCl}\\quad\\quad\\quad$ Triphenylphosphine","difficulty":"Hard","source":"VITEEE 2008","_marksId":"64e458c8ec226f2f4360a5cd"},{"id":116342,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Which of the following oxides is strongly basic?","options":["$\\mathrm{Tl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$","$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$","$\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$","$\\mathrm{Ga}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"On moving down the group, the nature of the oxides of group 13 elements changes from weakly acidic to amphoteric and amphoteric to basic. $\\mathrm{Tl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ in aqueous solution gives $\\mathrm{TlOH}$ which soluble and a strong base.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2014","_marksId":"64e45913ec226f2f4360a8b3"},{"id":116343,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"In $\\mathrm{XeF}_{2}, \\mathrm{XeF}_{4}, \\mathrm{XeF}_{6}$ the number of lone pairs on Xe are respectively","options":["$2,3,1$","$1,2,3$","$4,1,2$","$3,2,1$"],"answer":2,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252F6tqU6Cqgc-FZu5t5FK510-kHV_nso10S9_KsrT-8XlQ.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2F6tqU6Cqgc-FZu5t5FK510-kHV_nso10S9_KsrT-8XlQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2F6tqU6Cqgc-FZu5t5FK510-kHV_nso10S9_KsrT-8XlQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252FWchaUn0cb7n49LztiC8wWxkoA6_BbYfZ82vNBhSa52U.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https:/