ing back the reactants.\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{XeF}_{6}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{XeO}_{3}+6 \\mathrm{HF}\r\n","difficulty":"Hard","source":"VITEEE 2016","_marksId":"64e4592cec226f2f4360a9a7"},{"id":116345,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Xenon hexafluoride on partial hydrolysis produces compounds ' $\\mathrm{X}$ ' and ' $\\mathrm{Y}$ '. Compounds ' $\\mathrm{X}$ ', 'Y' and the oxidation state of $\\mathrm{Xe}$ are respectively:","options":["$\\mathrm{XeOF}_4(+6)$ and $\\mathrm{XeO}_3(+6)$","$\\mathrm{XeO}_2(+4)$ and $\\mathrm{XeO}_3(+6)$","$\\mathrm{XeOF}_4(+6)$ and $\\mathrm{XeO}_2 \\mathrm{~F}_2(+6)$","$\\mathrm{XeO}_2 \\mathrm{~F}_2(+6)$ and $\\mathrm{XeO}_2(+4)$"],"answer":2,"solution":"\n \\mathrm{XeF}_6+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\frac{\\text { partial }}{\\text { hydrolysis }} \\stackrel{+6}{\\mathrm{XeOF}_4}+2 \\mathrm{HF}\n\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252FMSI8WH0AQOIGaQbN5K8Y7ieyKHpuBqxA8HpAnulft_A.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FMSI8WH0AQOIGaQbN5K8Y7ieyKHpuBqxA8HpAnulft_A.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FMSI8WH0AQOIGaQbN5K8Y7ieyKHpuBqxA8HpAnulft_A.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2021","_marksId":"64e45959ec226f2f4360ab56"},{"id":116346,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"With excess of water, both $\\mathrm{P}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}$ and $\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ give","options":["$\\mat